{title: 321 - My Jesus, I Love Thee}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #321 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 321}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]My Je[Bb]sus, I [F]love Thee, I [C7]know Thou art [F]mine;
[F]For Thee [Bb]all the [F]follies of [C7]sin I re[F]sign.
[F]My gra[Bb]cious [F]Re[C7]dee[F]m[C]er, my [F]Sav[Bb]ior art [F]Th[C7]ou;
[F]If ev[Bb]er I [F]loved thee, my [C7]Jesus, 'tis [F]now.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]I [Bb]love thee [F]because thou [C7]hast first [F]loved me,
[F]and [Bb]purchased [F]my pardon [C7]on [F]Calvary's tree;
[F]I [Bb]love [F]thee [C7]for [F]wearing [C]the [F]thorns [Bb]on [F]thy [C7]brow;
[F]if [Bb]ever I [F]loved thee, [C7]my Jesus, [F]'tis now.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]I'll love [Bb]Thee in [F]life, I [C7]will love [F]Thee 'til death,
[F]And praise [Bb]Thee as [F]long as [C7]Thou lendest [F]me breath;
[F]And [Bb]say [F]when [C7]the [F]death [C]dew [F]lies [Bb]cold [F]on [C7]my brow,
[F]if [Bb]ever I [F]loved thee, [C7]my Jesus, [F]'tis now.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]In [Bb]mansions [F]of glory [C7]and [F]endless delight;
[F]I'll [Bb]ever adore [F]thee [C7]in heaven [F]so bright;
[F][Bb]I'll [F]sing [C7]with [F]the [C]glittering [F]crown [Bb]on [F]my [C7]brow;
[F]if [Bb]ever I [F]loved thee, [C7]my Jesus, [F]'tis now.
{end_of_verse}
